<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Overrides the .NET MAUI Android SDK's own default Maui.MainTheme (bundled inside the MAUI
      workload, not a file in this project) to fix a real crash hit on a physical device (Samsung
      Galaxy S23+, dark mode) the first time this app's Android head was ever actually launched —
      every cold start crashed with:

        java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: This component requires that you specify a valid
        TextAppearance attribute. Update your app theme to inherit from Theme.MaterialComponents.
          at com.google.android.material.navigation.NavigationBarView.<init>
          at com.google.android.material.bottomnavigation.BottomNavigationView.<init>
          at com.microsoft.maui.PlatformInterop.createNavigationBar
          at ShellItemRenderer.onCreateView

      Root cause: the SDK default Maui.MainTheme points bottomNavigationViewStyle at the OLD
      Android Design-support-library style (@style/Widget.Design.BottomNavigationView), which
      doesn't declare the itemTextAppearanceActive/Inactive attributes the actual widget being
      created — com.google.android.material.bottomnavigation.BottomNavigationView, used to render
      AppShell.xaml's TabBar on Android — requires. Fixed by pointing it at the real Material
      Components equivalent instead. Same resource name ("Maui.MainTheme") as the SDK's own
      definition, so Android's resource merger lets this project-level override win — standard,
      supported way to customize it, not a hack.
    -->
    <style name="Maui.MainTheme" parent="Maui.MainTheme.Base">
        <item name="bottomNavigationViewStyle">@style/SecureApp.BottomNavigationView</item>
    </style>

    <!--
      2026-10-05, user's own report: the bottom tab labels ("Nástěnka", "Nastavení", ...) wrap
      letter-by-letter on some phones but not others (fine on Petr Faltus's device, broken on the
      user's own) — same "no word-boundary to wrap at, container too narrow" class of bug already
      fixed once for the Akutní-stavy tiles. Root cause here: BottomNavigationView's default item
      text size is in sp, which scales with the DEVICE's own system font-size/accessibility setting
      (completely separate from this app's own in-app "Velikost písma", which doesn't touch native
      Shell tab labels at all) — on a phone with a larger system font scale, 5-6 Czech tab labels
      sharing the screen width no longer fit on one line. Fixing the text size in dp instead of sp
      makes it immune to that device setting entirely, matching this project's own established
      pattern of overriding Maui.MainTheme for the SAME widget (see the style above).
    -->
    <style name="SecureApp.BottomNavigationView" parent="Widget.MaterialComponents.BottomNavigationView">
        <item name="itemTextAppearanceActive">@style/SecureApp.BottomNavigationView.TextAppearance</item>
        <item name="itemTextAppearanceInactive">@style/SecureApp.BottomNavigationView.TextAppearance</item>
    </style>
    <style name="SecureApp.BottomNavigationView.TextAppearance" parent="TextAppearance.MaterialComponents.Caption">
        <item name="android:textSize">10dp</item>
    </style>
</resources>
